Actually — the issue may be CRLF/encoding: I wrote the file with Set-Content UTF8 (with BOM in Windows PowerShell 5!). BOM at start of .mjs → node handles BOM fine. The eval expression: multiline string in JS single backticks? I used `( `(()=>{...})()` )` — the JS template literal spans many lines including... AH WAIT: the expression contains NO backticks. Hmm.

Let me look for a real syntax error: 
```
(()=>{ 
  const q=document.querySelector('.obj'); if(!q) return {...};
  const r=q.getBoundingClientRect();
  ...
  return {x,y,hitId:el&&el.id,...};
})()
```
All balanced? `return {x,y,hitId:el&&el.id,hitCls:el&&el.className,hitTag:el&&el.tagName, bandDisplay:..., bandHidden:..., objRect:{l:r.left,t:r.top,w:r.width,h:r.height}})()` — count braces: outer obj closes with `}}` then `)` closes IIFE parens then `()` invoke... wait the IIFE is `(function(){...})()` — the call syntax: `})()`. I have `}})()`: first } closes objRect inner object {l:...}, second } closes the outer return object, then `)` closes function body paren `}`,... hmm let me count: IIFE opening: `(  ()=>{` — arrow fn parens + arrow + brace. Closing needs: `}` (fn body) + `)` (arrow param parens? arrow has empty params: `()`) — full close = `})()`. In my string end: `h:r.height}})()}`— that's `}}` (objRect + return obj) then `}` (fn body) + `)` (arrow group) + `()` invoke + `}` ← EXTRA brace closing the outer `(()=>{...})()` wrapper I wrapped the whole thing in! The evaljs call: evalRaw(`( ()=>{ ... } )()`) — I wrapped ANOTHER IIFE outside: `evalRaw(\`(()=>{  ... inner ... })()\`)`. The inner already had its own IIFE. So there's one `}` too many. In probe5 the same double-wrap existed → same SyntaxError → returned undefined. And probe4's big eval also double-wrapped?? probe4: `evaljs(\`(()=>{const q=...; ... return JSON.stringify({...})})()\`)` — single wrap, worked. OK.

